meta {
  name: 20 Logout
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Episode 12 — the cold open, and its fix.

  On camera:
    1. run "03 Me" → 200
    2. run this → "Logged out successfully."
    3. run "03 Me" again WITHOUT logging back in → 401

  Step 3 is the whole episode. Before the denylist existed, step 3 returned 200
  and the token kept working until it expired.

  Note it revokes BOTH: this access token (by its jti) and the user's refresh
  tokens. Closing one door is closing neither.
}
